 "purpose": "KV-PC2 10-19 (structurally safe successor of sr1 / sr2): KV-PC SAFE 10-19 (one failed route = structural redesign; terminal gate 1248d0585 PC WARN / PC_H FAIL): the five runtime-indexed flop arrays (front 32x297 = 9216 FF on 4 storage roots, tag queue 64x34, return ring 8x288, embedding CDC FIFOs 8x349 / 8x258) are 23 native 32x64 dual-clock SRAM banks (kv_pc_sram_gen / qkd_kvpc_sram_1019.sv; 0 added edges); the 2405 / 2051 / 854-load pointer roots are gone; scheduler hr_q / hgo are kept copy families split <= 32 loads (ot_rst_copies); front banks write AND read on hck (the landing / pointer clock: no storage-root clocks, no same-phase claim); return-ring banks write on hck, read on ck behind per-slot toggle 2-flop synchronisers; embedding FIFOs are Gray-pointer async FIFOs; the three dropped sticky faults (chain / es_merge / embr) leave registered on pc__hfx[2:0] for the health plane.",
